.TH LIBREGMAN 3 2026-10-19 "Peios peiosutils 0.8.18"
.SH NAME
libregman \- registry manual parsing and lookup library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <peios/regman.h>

.B "uint32_t peios_regman_abi_version(void);"
.B "peios_regman_result *peios_regman_parse(peios_regman_bytes source);"
.B "peios_regman_result *peios_regman_query(peios_regman_bytes directory, peios_regman_bytes index, uint32_t mode, peios_regman_bytes text);"
.B "int32_t peios_regman_fold(peios_regman_bytes text, uint8_t *out, size_t capacity, size_t *length);"
.B "void peios_regman_free(peios_regman_result *);"
.B "int32_t peios_regman_error(const peios_regman_result *);"
.B "peios_regman_bytes peios_regman_message(const peios_regman_result *);"
.B "size_t peios_regman_record_count(const peios_regman_result *);"
.B "size_t peios_regman_issue_count(const peios_regman_result *);"
.B "int32_t peios_regman_record(const peios_regman_result *, size_t index, peios_regman_record_view *);"
.B "int32_t peios_regman_issue(const peios_regman_result *, size_t index, peios_regman_issue_view *);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libregman
parses registry-manual fragments and searches installed manuals.
Parsing returns valid records alongside recoverable parse issues.
Inspect both record and issue counts after checking the operation error.
.PP
Queries use PEIOS_REGMAN_EXACT for one anchor, PEIOS_REGMAN_KEY for a key
and its documented values, or PEIOS_REGMAN_SEARCH for text search.
Query text is case-folded internally; search terms are separated by whitespace.
An absent directory or index selects its environment setting or default.
.PP
.B peios_regman_fold
case-folds UTF-8 text as manual names compare, the folding a query applies to
its text, so that a program can compare names the way the library does.
It writes the folded text to
.I out
and its length to
.IR length .
It returns zero, ERANGE with the length needed when
.I capacity
is too small, or EINVAL for text that is not UTF-8 or a null
.IR length .
A zero
.I capacity
with a null
.I out
asks only for the length.
Paths use raw Unix bytes, preserving filenames that are not UTF-8.
.PP
Record views contain the provider, source path, anchor, canonical name,
optional value metadata, body, and byte offset of the source fence.
An absent optional field differs from a present empty field.
Issue views report one-based source lines and diagnostic text.
Indexed getters return a POSIX error code and leave output untouched on failure.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Operations return an owned handle on success and on failure.
Check the matching error accessor before reading results; zero means success
and a nonzero value is a POSIX error number, independent of errno.
A diagnostic message is borrowed from a failed handle.
A null handle has error EINVAL and no message.
.PP
Free every handle exactly once with its matching free function, including
handles describing failed operations.
Freeing null is harmless.
Returned byte spans and record views remain valid only while their owning
handle remains alive.
Counts return zero for failed or null handles; check the error first.
.PP
Input byte spans are borrowed for the duration of the call.
A null pointer with zero length denotes absence; a non-null zero-length span
is an explicitly empty value.
Lengths exceeding the addressable Rust slice range and null pointers with
nonzero lengths are rejected.
Other non-null pointers must identify valid, readable allocations.
Output pointers and arrays must have the alignment required by their C type.
Text spans contain UTF-8 without a required terminating null byte.
.PP
Read-only access can occur concurrently.
Destruction requires exclusive ownership and ends all borrowed views.
Allocation exhaustion follows the Rust allocator's process-abort policy;
it is not reported as a recoverable ENOMEM result.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid spans, invalid UTF-8 text, an unknown query mode, a null required
handle or output pointer, or a malformed query.
.TP
.B ERANGE
An indexed getter requested an entry outside the available range.
.TP
.B ENOENT
No matching manual entry was found by a lookup operation.
.TP
.B EIO
Reading the manual corpus failed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REGMAN_DIR
Manual directory used when no explicit directory is supplied.
.TP
.B REGMAN_INDEX
Index path used when no explicit index is supplied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/regman
Default registry-manual directory.
.TP
.I /var/cache/regman/index
Default index cache.
.SH NOTES
The runtime SONAME is libregman.so.1 and the ABI version function returns 1.
Use the regman pkg-config module for compiler and linker options.
The Rust wrapper is the peios-regman crate.
.PP
Index lookup uses a validated owned snapshot.
An invalid index falls back to scanning manuals.
Replacing a previously read index does not change that snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR regman (1),
.BR libreg (3),
.BR libevman (3)
